<title>CHILE: Chile court orders delay in new power prices.</title>
<headline>Chile court orders delay in new power prices.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Chilean appeals court ruled that the government cannot fix new electricity distribution prices until a legal dispute between the government and power firms over the rates is resolved, said judicial sources.</p>
<p>Power companies including Chilectra have complained that the government acted illegally in the way it has set the new prices, which will be in force for the next four years.</p>
<p>The national energy commission has not given details publicly of the new prices, but they are widely believed to fall by around 10 percent.  </p>
<p>The government had planned to bring the new prices into force last Monday.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595 x212</p>
